{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018LUWR1k8yrNs7qRNedFmwW","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_4/projects/distrib_canary_collapse/literature_map.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"papers:\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  # CORE MODEL COLLAPSE\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"shumailov2024curse\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"The Curse of Recursion: Training on Generated Data Makes Models Forget\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Ilia Shumailov, Zakhar Shumaylov, Yiren Zhao, Yarin Gal, Nicolas Papernot, Ross Anderson\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"Nature\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.17493\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"core-collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"定义 model collapse 现象：迭代用合成数据替换真实数据训练会导致分布尾部消失\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"区分 early model collapse（尾部信息丢失）和 late model collapse（分布完全收敛）\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"三类误差来源：statistical approximation, functional expressivity, functional approximation，跨代复合\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"在 VAE、GMM、LLM 上均验证了 collapse 的普遍性\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"奠基论文，定义了我们研究的核心现象。我们的 canary 指标旨在提前检测其描述的 early collapse 阶段\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"perplexity\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"distributional tail mass\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"alemohammad2024mad\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Self-Consuming Generative Models Go MAD\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Sina Alemohammad, Josue Casco-Rodriguez, Lorenzo Luzi, Ahmed Imtiaz Humayun, Hossein Babaei, Daniel LeJeune, Ali Siahkoohi, Richard Baraniuk\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ICLR 2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.01850\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"core-collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"提出 Model Autophagy Disorder (MAD) 概念\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"autophagous loop 中没有足够新鲜真实数据时，质量或多样性必然渐进下降\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"在图像生成领域验证 self-consuming loop 的退化效应\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"MAD 框架与我们的 iterative loop 设置直接对应；其 quality vs diversity tradeoff 可能反映在不同 canary 指标上\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"FID\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"precision\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"recall\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"diversity\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"dohmatob2024tale\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"A Tale of Tails: Model Collapse as a Change of Scaling Laws\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Elvis Dohmatob, Yunzhen Feng, et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ICML 2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.07043\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"core-collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"通过 scaling laws 视角分析 model collapse：collapse 表现为 scaling law 的变化\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"发现 loss of scaling, shifted scaling, skill un-learning, grokking 等多种退化模式\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"混入少量干净数据可缓解 collapse 并引发 grokking 现象\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"在 transformer 算术任务和 Llama2 文本生成上验证\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"scaling law 变化视角为我们提供了理论基础；grokking 现象暗示 canary 指标可能出现非单调行为\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"test loss\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"scaling exponents\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"dohmatob2025strong\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Strong Model Collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Elvis Dohmatob, Yunzhen Feng, Arjun Subramonian, Julia Kempe\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ICLR 2025 (Spotlight)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.04840\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"core-collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"即使合成数据占比极小（1/1000），仍可导致 model collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"更大的训练集并不能避免 collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"更大的模型（random projection 近似下）反而可能放大 collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"存在 interpolation threshold 的 double-descent 现象\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"强化了早期检测的必要性——即使极小的合成数据比例也能触发 collapse，因此 canary 指标必须敏感\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"test loss\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"population risk\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"guo2024linguistic\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"The Curious Decline of Linguistic Diversity: Training Language Models on Synthetic Text\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Yanzhu Guo, Guokan Shang, et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"NAACL 2024 Findings\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.09807\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"core-collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"evaluation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"递归微调中，linguistic diversity 在连续迭代中持续下降\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"创造性任务中 diversity 下降最显著\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"开发了覆盖 lexical、syntactic、semantic 三层的 diversity 指标体系\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"其多层 diversity 指标体系可直接作为我们 canary 指标的候选集；创造性 vs 事实任务的差异可能影响 canary 灵敏度\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"distinct-n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"type-token ratio\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"syntactic diversity\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"semantic diversity\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"briesch2024selfconsuming\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Large Language Models Suffer From Their Own Output: An Analysis of the Self-Consuming Training Loop\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Martin Briesch, Dominik Sobania, Franz Rothlauf\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv (2311.16822)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.16822\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"core-collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"direct-competitor\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"首次系统研究 LLM 的 self-consuming training loop\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"full synthetic cycle（完全替换）导致单点 collapse；data augmentation cycle 导致 diversity 缓慢下降\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"expanding data cycle（累积）在 50 代内保持 diversity\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"其不同 data cycle 策略的对比直接对应我们的 alpha（synthetic ratio）实验设置\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"diversity\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"quality\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"truong2025entropy\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Entropy Collapse: A Universal Failure Mode of Intelligent Systems\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Truong Xuan Khanh, Truong Quynh Hoa\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv (2512.12381)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.12381\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"core-collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"theoretical-foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"证明 entropy collapse 是一阶（不连续）相变，临界点 α_c(β) = 1/(1−β)，entropy 在临界点跳变 0.698 nats\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"两个 universality class：Class 1（凸反馈，如 power-law）不可逆 ν=1；Class 2（线性反馈）可逆 ν=1/2\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"因为是一阶相变，autocorrelation/variance 等传统 early-warning signal 在 collapse 前保持有限——无预警\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"定义了 canary 失效的 regime boundary：Class 1 凸反馈系统中传统 canary 理论上无效。我们需证明我们的 canary 在 Class 2+ regime 或非纯反馈场景中有效\\\\\\\"\\\\n    gaps: \\\\\\\"理论框架高度抽象，未给出 LLM 具体场景下的 α/β 估计方法；未测试哪些 canary 在接近一阶相变时仍有部分预警能力\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"entropy\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"autocorrelation\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"variance\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"wang2026contaminated\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Can Generative Artificial Intelligence Survive Data Contamination? Theoretical Guarantees under Contaminated Recursive Training\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Kevin Wang, Hongqian Niu, Didong Li\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv (2602.16065)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.16065\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"core-collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"theoretical-foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"首个不限数据分布假设的正面理论结果：universal approximator 下 contaminated recursive training 仍可收敛\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"收敛速率 = min(baseline 模型收敛速率, 每轮真实数据比例)——真实数据比例是瓶颈\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"突破了先前仅限 discrete/Gaussian 分布的理论框架，适用于一般连续分布\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"为 post-MVP α-sweep 实验提供理论上界：收敛速率由 real data fraction 决定，可预测不同 α 下的 collapse 速率\\\\\\\"\\\\n    gaps: \\\\\\\"universal approximator 假设在实际有限容量模型中不严格成立；未讨论 canary 指标行为\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"convergence rate\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"population risk\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  # CANARY / EARLY WARNING METRICS\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"chen2025scales\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Characterizing Model Behavior Under Synthetic Data Training: An Empirical Study Across Scales and Mixing Ratios\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Anonymous\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv (2510.05133)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.05133\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"canary-metrics\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"direct-competitor\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"**Calibration degradation precedes accuracy loss** — ECE 是 collapse 的 early warning signal\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"20% synthetic data 以下性能稳定，30% 以上退化加速\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"大模型（6.9B-12B）比小模型（410M-1.4B）更鲁棒\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"推理任务比检索任务更易退化\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"iteration 1 + 30% synthetic 时 ECE 从 0.08 升至 0.14（+75%）\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"**最直接的竞争者/先驱**。证实 ECE 可作为 canary，但未做 lead-lag 分析，未建立多指标 panel 框架\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"ECE\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"accuracy\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"perplexity\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"gambetta2024surplexity\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Learning by Surprise: Surplexity for Mitigating Model Collapse in Generative AI\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Daniele Gambetta et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv (2410.12341)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.12341\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"canary-metrics\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"direct-competitor\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"提出 surplexity（model surprise 度量）同时用于检测 collapse 和过滤训练数据\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"用 semantic networks 分析文本重复性和语义多样性\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"用 next-token probability 定量衡量 diversity loss\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"高 surplexity 过滤策略至少与 human-data baseline 同效，且更能降低分布偏斜\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"不需要区分 human vs AI-generated data\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"surplexity 可作为我们 canary 指标候选之一；其 semantic network 方法提供了 diversity 度量的另一视角\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"surplexity\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"semantic network metrics\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"next-token probability\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"qiu2025spectral\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Spectral Alignment as Predictor of Loss Explosion in Neural Network Training\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Haiquan Qiu, You Wu, Yingjie Tan, Yaqing Wang, Quanming Yao\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv (2510.04202)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.04202\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"canary-metrics\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"method-component\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Spectral Alignment (SA) 监控层输入与权重矩阵主奇异向量的分布对齐\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"SA sign diversity collapse 是 representational collapse 和训练发散的早期预测器\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"比 weight norm、gradient norm 等传统指标更早、更清晰地检测到训练失败\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"健康层的 SA 应有正负均衡分布，collapse 到单侧则预示不稳定\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"SA 是潜在的高价值 canary 指标——专门设计为 early warning，可直接纳入我们的指标 panel\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"spectral alignment\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"weight norm\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"gradient norm\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"he2025closer\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"A Closer Look at Model Collapse: From a Generalization-to-Memorization Perspective\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Shiliang He et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"NeurIPS 2025 (Spotlight)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.16499\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"canary-metrics\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"direct-competitor\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"识别 diffusion model collapse 中的 generalization → memorization 转变\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"**训练数据的 entropy 递减是 collapse 的直接驱动因素和清晰指标**\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"提出基于 entropy 的数据选择策略，有效缓解 collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"data entropy 作为 canary 的有效性已被验证（diffusion domain）；需测试是否在 LLM 场景同样有效\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"entropy\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"FID\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"diversity\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"ba2024fill\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Fill In The Gaps: Model Calibration and Generalization with Synthetic Data\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Yang Ba, Michelle V Mancenido, Rong Pan\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"EMNLP 2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.10864\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"canary-metrics\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"background\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"用 LLM 生成合成数据来修复 calibration 错误的 reliability diagram bins\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"推导了基于 PAC 框架的 ECE bound\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"合成数据可改善 calibration 但需精心设计生成策略\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"ECE 的理论 bound 可为我们的 canary 阈值设定提供理论依据\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"ECE\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"accuracy\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"sigma2026spectral\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"SIGMA: Scalable Spectral Insights for LLM Model Collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Yi Gu, Lingyou Pang, Xiangkun Ye, Tianyu Wang, Jianyu Lin, Carey E. Priebe, Alexander Aue\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv (2601.03385)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.03385\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"canary-metrics\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"direct-competitor\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"基于 embedding Gram matrix 谱分析的 collapse 监控框架：Track I（确定性谱界）保守但鲁棒，Track II（随机谱缩放）灵敏但需采样\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Track I/II 的分歧本身是 early-stage collapse 的诊断信号，早于表面重复性伪影\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"随机谱界使部分观测的 Gram matrix 也可用于大规模模型的可扩展监控\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"最直接的 spectral canary 竞争者。我们的 effective rank 是其简化版（单一标量 vs 完整谱界）；需在 related work 中明确差异：SIGMA 提供双轨谱界，我们用单一 effective rank 换取更低计算开销和多指标 panel 集成\\\\\\\"\\\\n    gaps: \\\\\\\"未做 lead-lag 分析，未与 ECE/diversity 等非谱指标对比；Track I/II 的计算开销在 iterative loop 多轮场景下可能不可忽略\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"Gram matrix eigenspectrum\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"spectral norm bounds\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"kalinowski2026topology\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Monitoring Neural Training with Topology: A Footprint-Predictable Collapse Index\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Alexander Kalinowski\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv (2604.26984)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.26984\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"canary-metrics\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"background\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"提出基于 Modular Morse Homology Maintenance (MMHM) 的在线拓扑监控方案，增量更新避免每轮重建\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Collapse Index (CI) 组合多尺度拓扑特征，在 LLM fine-tuning 和 temporal KGE 训练中提供低延迟 early-warning\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"拓扑方法捕捉表示空间的各向异性和多尺度结构丧失\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"topology-based monitoring 是与 spectral 方法正交的 collapse 检测路线。我们排除了该方法（计算开销高、可解释性弱），但 related work 需要对比说明选择 spectral/calibration panel 而非 topology 的理由\\\\\\\"\\\\n    gaps: \\\\\\\"计算开销显著高于 effective rank 等标量指标；未在 iterative synthetic training loop 场景下测试；与 ECE 等轻量 canary 无对比\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"Collapse Index\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"persistent homology features\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  # DIVERSITY METRICS (BACKGROUND)\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"zhu2018texygen\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Texygen: A Benchmarking Platform for Text Generation Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Yaoming Zhu et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"SIGIR 2018\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2018\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.01886\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"canary-metrics\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"background\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"提出 Self-BLEU 度量：计算生成句子间的 BLEU 相似度，Self-BLEU 越高多样性越低\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"成为文本生成多样性评估的标准基准之一\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"Self-BLEU 是我们 diversity canary 的经典候选\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"Self-BLEU\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"BLEU\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"li2016diversity\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"A Diversity-Promoting Objective Function for Neural Conversation Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Jiwei Li et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"NAACL 2016\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2016\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1510.03055\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"canary-metrics\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"background\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"提出 distinct-1 / distinct-2 指标衡量生成文本的 n-gram 多样性\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"计算 unique n-gram 数占总 n-gram 数的比例\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"distinct-n 是最廉价的 diversity canary 之一，计算开销极低\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"distinct-1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"distinct-2\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  # REPRESENTATION / SPECTRAL COLLAPSE\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"jing2022understanding\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Understanding Dimensional Collapse in Contrastive Self-supervised Learning\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Li Jing et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ICLR 2022\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2022\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=YevsQ05DEN7\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"canary-metrics\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"method-component\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"定义 dimensional collapse：embedding 向量只跨越低维子空间\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"effective rank（基于归一化特征值 entropy 的指数）作为 collapse 度量\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"strong augmentation 和 implicit regularization 驱动低秩解\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"effective rank 的定义和计算方式可直接迁移到我们的 embedding 空间监控\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"effective rank\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"singular value spectrum\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"noci2024mind\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Mind the Gap: A Spectral Analysis of Rank Collapse and Signal Propagation in Transformers\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Lorenzo Noci et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"NeurIPS 2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.07799\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"canary-metrics\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"method-component\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"用 Random Matrix Theory 分析 attention 层的 rank collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"发现 attention matrix 最大两个奇异值之间的 spectral gap 是 width-collapse 的根因\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"rank collapse in depth: 所有 token 沿层收敛到单一表示\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"spectral gap 作为另一种 spectral canary 候选；其 RMT 分析框架可启发我们的理论工作\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"spectral gap\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"singular values\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"effective rank\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  # DATA MIXING & ACCUMULATION\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"kazdan2025collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Collapse or Thrive? Perils and Promises of Synthetic Data in a Self-Generating World\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Joshua Kazdan, Rylan Schaeffer, Apratim Dey, Matthias Gerstgrasser, Rafael Rafailov, David L. Donoho, Sanmi Koyejo\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ICML 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.16713\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"data-mixing\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"系统对比 replace vs accumulate 场景\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"replace → collapse；accumulate → 可避免 collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"发现 real data 和 synthetic data 之间存在非平凡的交互效应\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"synthetic data 的价值取决于 real data 的绝对数量\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"直接对应我们的 alpha（mixing ratio）实验维度；其 replace vs accumulate 框架是我们实验设计的重要参考\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"test loss\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"dey2024breaking\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Is Model Collapse Inevitable? Breaking the Curse of Recursion by Accumulating Real and Synthetic Data\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Apratim Dey, David Donoho, et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ICML 2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.01413\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"data-mixing\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"替换数据 → 发散 population risk；累积数据 → 避免发散\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"证明累积策略在多种模型（GMM, HMM, LLM）上有效\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"为我们的 alpha 实验提供理论预测：累积 vs 替换是 collapse 速率的关键调节因子\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"population risk\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"epstein2024howbad\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"How Bad is Training on Synthetic Data? A Statistical Analysis of Language Model Collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Mohamed El Amine Epstein et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv (2404.05090)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.05090\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"data-mixing\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"background\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"纯合成数据训练不可避免 collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"给出 synthetic data 比例上界的估计——低于此比例可避免 collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"递归训练使原始分布尾部消失\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"其 mixing ratio 上界估计可对比我们实验中观测到的 canary 触发阈值\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"perplexity\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"fu2025selfconsuming\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"A Theoretical Perspective: How to Prevent Model Collapse in Self-consuming Training Loops\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Shi Fu, Yingjie Wang, Yuzhu Chen, Xinmei Tian, Dacheng Tao\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ICLR 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.18865\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"data-mixing\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"theoretical-foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"引入 recursive stability 概念，首次给出 self-consuming loop 的泛化分析\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"恒定比例的真实数据即可保证 STL 收敛；同时给出最优合成数据量的 insight\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"模型架构和 real/synthetic 数据比例共同决定 STL 的成败\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"为 post-MVP α-sweep（synthetic ratio 梯度）实验提供理论预期：50% accumulation 条件下收敛有理论保证\\\\\\\"\\\\n    gaps: \\\\\\\"理论分析限于特定 generalization bound 框架，未涉及 canary 指标的行为；未讨论不同 α 下 collapse 速率的精细结构\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"generalization bound\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"population risk\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"bakshi2026improvement\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"From Collapse to Improvement: Statistical Perspectives on the Evolutionary Dynamics of Iterative Training on Contaminated Sources\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Soham Bakshi, Sunrit Chakraborty\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv (2602.10531)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.10531\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"data-mixing\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"theoretical-foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"αt（每轮混合权重）trajectory 和 nt（每轮样本量）scaling 的交互决定三种 regime：collapse / improvement / consistency\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"当 αt 衰减足够快且 nt 增长足够快时，迭代估计可收敛到真实分布（improvement regime）\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"αt 衰减不足或 nt 增长不足则进入 collapse regime；边界条件给出 consistency regime\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"在 next-token prediction 语言模型上分析完整迭代演化动态\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"αt/nt 条件直接对应我们 α-sweep 实验的理论预期：不同 synthetic ratio 衰减曲线下 canary 应呈现不同时序模式\\\\\\\"\\\\n    gaps: \\\\\\\"理论结果基于渐近分析，有限代数下的 transient behavior 未充分刻画；未讨论哪些指标能区分三种 regime\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"population risk\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"total variation distance\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  # MITIGATION & VERIFICATION\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"feng2025escaping\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Escaping Model Collapse via Synthetic Data Verification\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Yunzhen Feng et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"NeurIPS 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.16657\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"data-mixing\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"background\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"通过外部 verifier（human 或 better model）注入信息可避免 collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"verifier-guided retraining 带来短期改善，但最终收敛到 verifier 的 knowledge center\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"除非 verifier 完全可靠，早期收益会 plateau 甚至逆转\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"verification 作为 intervention 策略——如果 canary 触发，可考虑此类 reactive intervention\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"test loss\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"barzilai2025consistency\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"When Models Don't Collapse: On the Consistency of Iterative MLE\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Daniel Barzilai, Ohad Shamir\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ICML 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.19046\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"core-collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"background\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"在标准 MLE 一致性假设下，即使 real data fraction 趋近零也可避免 collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"但证明了某些情况下 collapse 可以任意快地发生——首次给出严格 collapse 反例\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"理论上的 collapse 可发生任意快的结论强化了 early warning 的价值\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: []\\\\n\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"dces2026counter\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Countering Model Collapse in Iterative Self-Training via Dynamic Center-Edge Sampling\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Anonymous\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"MDPI Electronics (2026)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://www.mdpi.com/2079-9292/15/4/869\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"data-mixing\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"background\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"提出 DCES（dynamic center-edge sampling）数据选择框架\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"DCES 在 ECE（0.1058 vs 0.1200）和 entropy 保持上优于随机选择\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"其 ECE 和 entropy 对比数据为我们的指标 baseline 提供参考\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"ECE\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"entropy\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  # POSITION / SURVEY / EPISTEMICS\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"schaeffer2025position\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Position: Model Collapse Does Not Mean What You Think\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Rylan Schaeffer, Joshua Kazdan, Alvan Caleb Arulandu, Sanmi Koyejo\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv (2503.03150)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.03150\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"core-collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"background\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"文献中实际包含 8 种不同且有时矛盾的 model collapse 定义\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"许多 collapse 预测依赖于与现实不符的假设\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"多种 collapse 场景是可以轻易避免的\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"提醒我们明确定义 collapse 的操作标准；不同定义可能需要不同的 canary 指标\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: []\\\\n\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"wang2025epistemic\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Epistemic Diversity and Knowledge Collapse in Large Language Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Wang et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv (2510.04226)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.04226\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"core-collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"background\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"27 个 LLM 在 155 个主题上的 epistemic diversity 评估\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"所有模型的 epistemic diversity 低于基本 web 搜索\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"模型越大 epistemic diversity 反而越低；RAG 有正面效果\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"knowledge collapse 维度可扩展我们对 diversity canary 的理解——不仅是 lexical/syntactic 还有 epistemic\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: [\\\\\\\"epistemic diversity\\\\\\\"]\\\\n\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  # METHODOLOGY (GRANGER / LEAD-LAG)\\\\n  # ============================================================\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"shojaie2022granger\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Granger Causality: A Review and Recent Advances\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Ali Shojaie, Emily B. Fox\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"Annual Review of Statistics and Its Application\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2022\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2105.02675\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"methodology\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"method-component\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Granger causality 综述：从经典线性到非线性/neural 方法\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Panel data 场景的 Granger causality 扩展\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"VAR 和 neural Granger causality 的对比\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"为我们的 panel Granger causality 分析提供方法论基础\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: []\\\\n\\\\n  - id: \\\\\\\"marcinkevics2022neural\\\\\\\"\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Granger Causality Using Neural Networks\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Raphael Marcinkevics, Julia Vogt\\\\\\\"\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv (2208.03703)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2022\\\\n    url: \\\\\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.03703\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"methodology\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"method-component\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_findings:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"用 neural network 估计 Granger causality，突破线性假设\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"两个模型对比法：含/不含外生变量的预测误差差异即 Granger causality 证据\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance_to_us: \\\\\\\"我们的多指标时序可能存在非线性关系，neural Granger causality 是自然选择\\\\\\\"\\\\n    metrics_studied: []\\\\n\\\\ngaps:\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"无人系统做过 canary 指标的 lead-lag / Granger causality 分析——现有工作只在事后观察到指标变化，未量化哪些指标能提前多少步预测 collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"ECE 在 collapse 场景下几乎未被系统研究——chen2025scales 是唯一报告 ECE 先于 accuracy 退化的工作，但未做因果分析\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"embedding effective rank 未在 iterative synthetic training 场景下被测试——仅在 contrastive learning/transformer 训练中研究过\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"多指标 panel 框架缺失——无人同时追踪 ECE + effective rank + diversity + perplexity 的时序行为并分析其 lead-lag 关系\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"alpha（synthetic ratio）对 canary 灵敏度的影响未被研究——现有工作只关注 alpha 对最终性能的影响，不关注 canary 的 lead time 如何随 alpha 变化\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"predictive intervention vs reactive intervention 缺少对比——没有工作量化 early warning 带来的实际干预收益\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"surplexity 和 spectral alignment 未在 iterative collapse 场景下交叉验证\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - \\\\\\\"跨任务 canary 普适性未知——reasoning vs retrieval vs creative tasks 中哪些 canary 更可靠\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nnovelty_assessment: |\\\\n  我们项目的核心 novelty 在于：\\\\n\\\\n  1. **Panel Granger Causality 框架**：首次将多指标时序数据的因果分析方法应用于 model collapse 早期预警。\\\\n     现有工作（chen2025scales, gambetta2024surplexity）只是事后观察到某些指标先变化，\\\\n     但没有人做过系统的 lead-lag 量化分析。\\\\n\\\\n  2. **多指标 Canary Panel**：同时追踪 ECE、effective rank、Self-BLEU/distinct-n、\\\\n     perplexity、entropy、surplexity 等指标，分析其相互关系和各自的 lead time。\\\\n     现有工作都是单一指标或最多两三个指标的孤立分析。\\\\n\\\\n  3. **alpha-dependent Canary Sensitivity**：系统研究 synthetic ratio 如何影响各 canary\\\\n     指标的灵敏度和 lead time。dohmatob2025strong 证明极小的 alpha 就能触发 collapse，\\\\n     但没人研究 canary 在不同 alpha 下的行为。\\\\n\\\\n  4. **与已有工作的差异**：\\\\n     - vs chen2025scales: 他们发现 ECE 先退化但没有做因果分析；我们用 Granger causality 量化\\\\n     - vs gambetta2024surplexity: 他们提出 surplexity 用于检测和缓解 collapse；\\\\n       我们将其纳入更广的 panel 并研究其 lead-lag 特性\\\\n     - vs he2025closer: 他们在 diffusion 中用 entropy 作为指标；我们在 LLM 中测试更多指标\\\\n     - vs qiu2025spectral: 他们的 SA 用于训练 loss explosion 预警；\\\\n       我们将类似思路迁移到 iterative collapse 场景\\\\n\\\\n  5. **潜在风险**：chen2025scales 已经非常接近我们的方向。如果他们扩展到 lead-lag 分析，\\\\n     我们的 novelty 会被削弱。需要快速推进并在方法论（Granger causality）上建立壁垒。\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 24089, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012yWLYgBCk3VMDoz7DN1r6R","session_id":"8b658381-150c-4d7a-982d-1cebf7ec2b62","uuid":"61acfe94-b1cb-481a-8030-ff21260816f6","timestamp":"2026-05-14T19:22:08.038Z"}
